qdev-host (0.5.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Hardware panel: through the TCP 8006 gateway the panel's requests use the
    page's credentials mode, so the browser sends them on the page's own
    connections. On a page opened by IP address with the certificate's
    warning accepted (the certificate names the node), Chrome rejected the
    certificate on the separate connections of requests without credentials,
    and the panel showed "Failed to fetch". The service still authorises
    only the Authorization header and ignores the PVE cookie.

 -- Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 09:40:00 +0200

qdev-host (0.5.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Hardware panel behind QSM Direct's TCP 8006 gateway: one failed or
    timed-out request, or an error page of HAProxy, no longer moves the page
    to the service's own port 8017, where the browser had often not accepted
    the certificate and the row asked to accept it. Only pveproxy answering
    /qdev-host/ (a gateway without the route) does; other failures are
    retried once and the next refresh uses the gateway again. The error row
    says which way failed, the hint about the certificate is shown only for
    port 8017, and failed requests are logged to the browser console.
  * The node service marks its answers with X-QDev-Host and exposes Server
    and X-QDev-Host to the panel on port 8017 too.
  * The panel's GET reads the VM config from pmxcfs (pending changes applied,
    as qm config prints it) and the running state from the pid file, as
    qemu-server does, instead of starting qm twice: about 0.2 s instead of
    1.3 s per refresh. Changes still go through qm.
  * qdev-host: plugin ABI v2 host side (guest RAM regions with fd/offset,
    quiesce/resume, host services from plugin threads, plugin damage, cursor
    plane, QDP_RESET_EXIT), the vendored libvfio-user with the patches it
    needs, --control socket, --qemu-qmp input relay, NOFILE limit as QEMU.
    v1 plugins (tb-vga) are unchanged. The apple-pvg plugin is in the source
    tree and needs QMetal (QMETAL_INCLUDE); it is not in this package.

 -- Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0200

qdev-host (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * virgl-gpu on NVIDIA: the GPU unit allows /dev/nvidia*, which NVIDIA's EGL
    opens next to the render node, and gives the driver a shader cache
    directory. Without them vhost-user-gpu exited with "Failed to initialize
    virgl" when the guest driver loaded, and QEMU then logged
    "failed to read msg header" without end.
  * A primary virgl-gpu is refused, with the way out, for a VM on the native
    shared display of the older QSM preview (dbus-display), which qemu-server
    does not start without a graphical Display.
  * A second device on the same PCIe root port is refused: a root port has
    one slot.

 -- Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 17:10:00 +0200

qdev-host (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Hardware panel: Edit (button or double click) on a qdev-host row changes
    the device's plugin arguments, KMS output, Display1 export and
    persistence; a vfio-user device of a running VM is unplugged and plugged
    again with the new settings. API: PUT /api/v1/vms/VMID/devices/ID;
    shell: qdevctl set VMID ID.
  * New built-in plugin virgl-gpu: a virtio-gpu with VirGL 3D acceleration
    whose rendering runs in QEMU's own vhost-user-gpu process
    (qdev-host-vugpu@.service) on a chosen render node. It is on the QEMU
    command line from the next VM start, because QEMU's D-Bus display only
    exports consoles that exist at start. As the primary display
    (vhost-user-vga) it replaces the VM's display device and QSM Direct's
    in-process VirGL GPU until it is removed. qdev-host gives the VM shared
    memory (memory-backend-memfd) unless it has hugepages or virtiofs; the
    pre-start hook stops a start whose memory no longer matches.

 -- Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 17:30:00 +0200

qdev-host (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Proxmox VE web UI behind QSM Direct's TCP 8006 gateway: qdev-host-pve
    ships a route for qsm-pve-direct-gateway (/qdev-host/ -> 127.0.0.1:8017,
    port from /etc/qdev-host/ui.json), and the Hardware panel uses the page's
    own origin when the page reports the gateway, so a browser that reaches
    only port 8006 needs no TCP 8017.  With an older gateway, or without one,
    the panel uses port 8017 as before.

 -- Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:45:00 +0200

qdev-host (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Proxmox VE web UI: the Hardware-panel overlay is now a pve-ui-overlays
    descriptor (/usr/share/pve-ui-overlays/overlays.d/qdev-host.json); the
    package no longer diverts index.html.tpl itself. Depends: pve-ui-overlays.
  * query-pci: report the secondary bus of hot-plugged devices (01:00.0).

